            },
            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "I love the idea of TutorMini!\r\n\r\nIn the meanwhile, on a more practical note, I've build a couple of coding agent skills to efficiently search Neovim/Minimax docs/config file (just a few lines pointing to the location of help files).\r\n\r\nhttps://gist.github.com/S1M0N38/1963facaf2add03d52edfd3fdbccba91\r\n\r\nIt's not a substitution for a proper Tutor but just a quick way to ask how to do certain stuff (I find it especially useful cuz I'm moving from another distro to MiniMax so I know that Neovim/MiniMax can do something 99% of the time but I need to learn new keymaps). ",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I love the idea of TutorMini!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In the meanwhile, on a more practical note, I've build a couple of coding agent skills to efficiently search Neovim/Minimax docs/config file (just a few lines pointing to the location of help files).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://gist.github.com/S1M0N38/1963facaf2add03d52edfd3fdbccba91\">https://gist.github.com/S1M0N38/1963facaf2add03d52edfd3fdbccba91</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It's not a substitution for a proper Tutor but just a quick way to ask how to do certain stuff (I find it especially useful cuz I'm moving from another distro to MiniMax so I know that Neovim/MiniMax can do something 99% of the time but I need to learn new keymaps).</p>",
